WEBVTT

NOTE English captions for https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rb2EkzjgO98, from YouTube, repeats removed.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.700
Assalamualaikum,

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:02.780
warahmatullah wabarakatuh.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.840
I want to thank you for joining me for this short series in this blessed month

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.660
of Ramadan.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.560
Inshallah ta'ala, this month is about spiritual elevation.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.980
It's about deeper understanding

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.640
of our relationship with Allah subhana wa ta'ala and with the Rasul sallallahu alaihi wa sallam.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.640
A deep part of Ramadan is gaining deeper insight

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.760
into how Allah subhana wa ta'ala blesses us, how we are to get close to Allah

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.880
subhana wa ta'ala,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.980
and deeper understanding of who we are as people and who we should aspire to be

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.060
as believers.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.440
Inshallah, over these next few videos, I'm going to be taking you through

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.920
a well-known collection of short, beautiful phrases

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.300
that have been crafted and written by none other than Ibn Ata'illah al-Iskandari.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:56.120
This book is known as al-Hikam, which just means these aphorisms or these short sayings that

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.420
are filled with wisdom

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.660
and a lot for us to think about.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.640
The words are short, but the meanings are deep.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:03.860
And inshallah,

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.460
I thank you for joining me for these gems of reflection

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:08.640
and depth

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.380
uh through the insight of Ibn Ata'illah al-Iskandari.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:18.000
So, with that said, inshallah, we're going to move into our first one for today, inshallah

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:18.640
ta'ala.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.080
Ibn Ata'illah, he says,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.160
Rubbama waradat al-dhuluma alaik

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.980
li yu'arrifaka qadra manna bihi

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:28.980
alaik.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.140
The Imam, he says

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:32.900
that sometimes

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.860
darkness will come over our heart.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.800
May- maybe it's a sin that we fall into.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.260
Uh maybe it's a emotional state that we're feeling.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.000
Um any type of darkness will come over our hearts.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.160
And we struggle with wondering why we are experiencing that.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.100
We struggle to wonder and understand

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.740
what is the wisdom behind it, right?

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.060
Um there's a hadith that is quite beautiful.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.600
In which the Rasul alayhi salaat wa salaam, he said that the believer's affair is quite

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:05.240
unique.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.580
If hardship comes,

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:11.040
the believer is patient, and that is good.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:16.040
And if ease comes, the believer is grateful, and that is also good.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.460
What the Prophet alayhi salaat wa salaam was teaching us in this Hadith is that

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.940
it's all good, as we used to say.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.120
It's all good.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.400
Meaning whatever we're going through, there is something there for us to notice.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.460
Something for us to learn.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.520
Some way for us to grow.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.940
And so, in this aphorism, in this Hikam,

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.560
the Imam, he says,

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:38.380
that

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.380
sometimes darkness will come over your heart.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.720
It comes in different ways.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:46.419
But why?

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.700
He says one of the reasons is

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.460
li yu'arrifaka qadra ma manna bihi alayk.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.320
So that he can make you recognize, so that he can make you see

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.000
the value of the blessings that he has given you before.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.520
Now, there's a few ways to look at this.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.320
There's a saying, you know, like faqidu shay, like a person that doesn't know one realizes

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.400
the blessing of something until it is taken away, until it is gone.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.700
What the Imam is saying here is

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:17.900
sometimes

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.020
you may fall into a sin.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:25.400
But the reason you fell into the sin is that Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala wants you

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.740
to realize how blessed you were when you were not caught in that sin.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.219
Maybe you go through a moment of some slight depression or some anxiety.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.040
But what is a deeper reason?

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.920
Or what What is it different a deeper wisdom?

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.740
Is that you walk away from that appreciating

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:41.920
the moments

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.200
of ease,

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.540
of of mental well-being.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.460
And here's what's even more profound.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.500
Our life is always going through ups and downs.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.240
That is the nature of the believer's life.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.680
And that's why I quoted the Hadith of the Rasul earlier on.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.440
But here's the deal.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.940
You may be in a dark moment right now.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.160
But the truth about life is there's constant change.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.020
That's the only

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:10.620
uh constant of life is change, quite ironically.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.400
So, when the blessings do return,

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.640
now you have a deeper appreciation for them.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.860
And so, as scholars have said, they said subhanallah,

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.340
when you look at it from this perspective,

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:29.140
the nikmah, hardship, has now become a ni'mah, a blessing.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.140
So, the idea is we don't want to fall into sin.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:36.120
But when we fall into sin, we have to have the ability to bounce back.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.240
And in order to bounce back, you have to see what was God teaching me through

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.439
this. What was I supposed to get out of this?

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.040
And that's what the Imam is teaching us.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.140
He says, "Rubbama,

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:47.380
sometimes,

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.100
darkness will come over the heart.

00:04:50.919 --> 00:04:53.300
And the reason that that may be coming

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.300
is so that you can gain a deeper appreciation

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:01.460
for the blessings that he has been constantly giving you before this hardship.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.900
And here's where it's so profound.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.100
The blessings that will come after this hardship.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.380
Our job is to become people that don't lose hope when the hardship comes.

00:05:12.919 --> 00:05:14.480
That we don't feel hopeless.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.700
We don't feel forsaken.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.140
But we realize that there's a blessing

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:18.860
in

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.780
every situation that we have gone through.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:24.220
So, if you're going through a hardship right now,

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:29.180
struggling with a sin, struggling to get back on your deen, maybe it's a family difficulty,

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:33.460
remember that this allows you to become someone of appreciation

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.020
and recognition.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.820
Now, last thing I'll say before we end today's session,

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.980
there's no greater blessing

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.080
than to be someone who recognizes the blessings that they have.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:50.240
That is the greatest blessing because to be a grateful person, shaqir,

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.620
you first have to recognize the blessings.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.620
And if we look throughout the entire Quoran, and if we look at the entire

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.980
Sunnah of the Rasul, why did he do what he did?

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.440
Why did he spend nights in prayer?

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:05.760
He said one reason.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:11.820
Li akuna abdan shaqura, so that I can become a person of gratitude.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:15.740
Everything we're doing in this month of Ramadan is based in gratitude.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.520
And there's no way to be grateful unless you value the blessings you have.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:22.880
And sometimes you only value

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:24.439
the light

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.120
because of the dark.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.400
May Allah bless you in your moments

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:33.580
and bring you light, contentment, and blessings in this blessed month of Ramadan.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.180
Salam alaykum wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuh.
